implementationPlan.description:
docs/SCHEMA.md: rewrite the stale WorkerType NOTE (stale since task-0b40957c). With the Edit tool, replace the two column-0 lines under `type WorkerType =` that start `// NOTE: the daemon cannot see which CLI a worker runs —` and `// record every worker as 'CLAUDE' today;` with exactly these seven column-0 lines:
// NOTE: worker.type is the CLI a seat reports; the daemon cannot check which CLI really runs.
// The launchers (scripts/moe-agent.{sh,ps1}) export MOE_WORKER_TYPE from the CLI they start:
// CLAUDE, CODEX, GEMINI or GROK (any other command is CLAUDE). moe-proxy adds it as workerType
// to claim_next_task and join_team unless the call sets its own. The daemon keeps an exact,
// case-sensitive name and records any other value as 'CLAUDE'. An omitted workerType keeps an
// existing record's type and makes a new record 'CLAUDE'. A governor record that
// enter_governance rebuilds after a purge is 'CLAUDE' until the seat reports again.
Nothing else in the file changes: the four union lines stay as landed (including cb378fd8's GEMINI comment), as does the blank line before `type WorkerStatus`.
Trace every claim to code and record the landed file:line for the summary (DoD 2). The edc3e937 lines are below; re-read them at the tip, because task-c199e177 shifts the launcher lines:
(1) reported, not verified: WORKER_TYPE_SCHEMA joinTeam.ts:41-46, plus docs/MCP_SERVER.md 'Informational only: it is unauthenticated'.
(2) launcher export: moe-agent.sh:632-647 (CLI_TYPE from the command's base name, the `case` sets MOE_WORKER_TYPE, `export`) and moe-agent.ps1:1219-1231 ($cliType.ToUpperInvariant()); c199e177 adds `agy` to the gemini branch of both.
(3) any other command is CLAUDE: sh `*) MOE_WORKER_TYPE=CLAUDE`; ps1 default `$cliType = "claude"` (:1220).
(4) moe-proxy: utils.ts:289 WORKER_TYPE_TOOLS (CLAIM_TOOL plus the join_team spellings), :302-322 injectWorkerType (a blank env sends nothing :307; the caller's own key wins :316), called at index.ts:734.
(5) exact name else CLAUDE: joinTeam.ts:9 WORKER_TYPES, :12-14 normalizeWorkerType.
(6) omitted: refreshWorkerType returns on undefined (joinTeam.ts:28); new records get normalizeWorkerType(params.workerType) at joinTeam.ts:79 and claimNextTask.ts:829.
(7) governor rebuild: enterGovernance.ts:89-91 `type: 'CLAUDE'`, refreshed by the next join_team (joinTeam.ts:97) or claim_next_task (claimNextTask.ts:484/:508).
Error handling: if a claim does not hold at the landed tip, reword only that clause. Keep the lead-in '// NOTE: worker.type', the column-0 `// ` form and the tokens the gate requires (MOE_WORKER_TYPE, workerType, claim_next_task, join_team, moe-proxy, CODEX, GEMINI, GROK, 'CLAUDE'), and say what changed in the summary. The text above matches no pattern the SCHEMA.md doc-contract tests forbid (util/daemonGitDocs.test.ts NEVER_RUNS_GIT; util/taskTimeBudgetDocs.test.ts seed/budget/check+firstClaimAt|wallClockMs), so do not add such words.

Verification, run ONCE after steps 1-2, from this task's worktree root in WSL bash (xmllint is /usr/bin/xmllint; Git Bash has none): executionContract.checkRefs[0], verbatim. Its fresh output is the complete_task verification (command = that text, exitCode 0, outputTail). Expect last line `OK`, exit 0; the dry run took about 0.3 s, far under the 20-minute gate budget.
What it checks, in order:
- B = MERGE_HEAD during a LANDING-RETRY merge, else the merge base with MOE_LAND_TARGET;
- the label L from MoeBundle.properties is set, is not Gemini, and matches the VS Code quick pick;
- plugin.xml is well-formed XML (xmllint) and package.json parses (node require);
- no 'Gemini' is left in either file;
- each file with ', L ' mapped back to ', Gemini CLI ' is byte-identical to B's copy (every other word unchanged);
- SCHEMA.md minus the WorkerType block's column-0 // lines equals B's;
- the new note starts '// NOTE: worker.type', has no 'reserved' remnant and holds the 9 tokens;
- `git diff --name-only $B` is exactly the three files.
Dry-run in a clone with cb378fd8's labels simulated: RED before the edits (it prints the three Gemini lines), GREEN after them, 14 mutants red, and the resume path green only through MERGE_HEAD.
Error handling for a red run (fix the text, never the check):
- printed Gemini lines: a replacement was missed;
- `cmp: - /dev/fd/63 differ: byte N, line M`: another byte of that file changed;
- a `diff` hunk: SCHEMA.md changed outside the NOTE lines;
- a bare token name: the note lacks it;
- rc=1 with no output: the label check, the lead-in, a 'reserved' remnant or the file scope (`git diff --name-only $B`).
- A red label check is a cb378fd8 problem: moe.report_blocked, not an edit.
QA re-run: in a clone detached at the completion sha with MOE_LAND_TARGET=<sha>^ exported (mem:decision-doc-row-checkrefs-worktree-mode). On the control checkout without it, B is HEAD, which already holds the change, so the map-back cmp is red by design.
